The included setup is ready to go. Start in second, find a rhythm with the throttle and practise catching and unwinding the wheel. Third is waiting when you are.

The default setup remains your starting point. Pressures affect response and temperature; more pressure does not always mean less grip. Anti-roll bars change front/rear balance, slow dampers change how weight settles, and the LSD controls how the rear wheels work together. Adjust matching left and right settings together, one setting at a time. If you lose your way, reset to the included defaults.

The Trueno keeps its rear axle alignment fixed.
